    {
      "sha256": "77357dbdaba34183181a2940a8cdce735aae457d5f4694b620c0fe81799c73b6",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "## Required Inputs"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "2122acceb06bd4b1bf7417ac3a53e769e73054d9f4cdda4e919cdf602424d6b0",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- any sources or alternatives that must be compared"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "3d4b9f171064970a2e9947e6e3f0fb13501d9ced9a9ac9ebe2cde123882829ec",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "## Required Output"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "c34906b1f1c3c14200786d7b39a7be48ac5a703827301490b4f5a4403f82b6e1",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "Every substantial response must include:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "462e9be0d37f75775aa7ed83727f4dcb0fd9230c0bc97de76e74570491f5235a",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not stack heavy frameworks concurrently without reason."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "a2f7f47b666b82ba7c10897612176fbd0471d4fca921c95c12e2b5a4278d7dbc",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not bloat the answer with every module when a smaller route is enough."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "153f329d96f6adbcea8f255559fb58d818927fab0b7f0676abe34aa0d479a1e3",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not pretend the model knows user preferences it has not been given."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8c515a3b2167ad8b14392932b090365fbbd89fd5f6de946ca68b9db950635dd1",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not turn grading into generic praise."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8712b04aee80d8dffe104a3044e827a94e0599d183fe2eceafefbddb98d6e2bf",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not claim orchestration, approval, or runtime delegation authority."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "084b828b0f657abc4e698fe7606bc3516d294be734e8ac16c8f0ecfd870dda10",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If the user asks for help, respond with the `HELP OUTPUT` section only:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "de5efcdb1dddd453ec5759a260623c1a73c12770bb439b233916be1ed95fca61",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If the user asks for examples, respond with the `HELP EXAMPLES OUTPUT` section only:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "e3aaf81fa3ff36a0e1f4c1101a863e1995a462a9d0114659c5a0384bab583c7e",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If the user asks for details, respond with the `MODULE REFERENCE` section only:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "30cc96828a95fb2b7fc65caf7a573af5a292616197d5ee766ae9bae413dc3f5b",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "1. `/stop` wins over every other command, exits active modes, and returns only the stop acknowledgement."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "62fdbfab6cff2658db8e92527f8b56861fb3173f1e73d96ff2beba303fedfe0a",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "3. Help, examples, and details are terminal only when neither stop command is present; return the one matching section and do not execute examples or modules."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "b3185ff1ce015a61822b3cd67bd75ee6eba8642e5ce367020b18727220d1e368",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "4. If more than one help, examples, or details control appears, ask the user to choose one instead of combining section-only outputs."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "8c1ae20069e89963464c29a0712934709cc957a0f0a827363cc392066e60b86c",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If multiple commands appear, SuperCharge MUST treat them as a stack and execute them as a multi-pass sequence."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "1853e84b2bca0eca1146342971f5af087edb4b71146959543ed688f95377268e",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If `/route` appears anywhere in the invocation, SuperCharge MUST print exactly one line first:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "bb919709e8475a0b190580085a5e756421b6c5d71ccedfd656c43937fdf314bf",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Never invent facts. If critical info is missing:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "f2dc3f65db6864bfc8c5148e6b50bc667f6dffa6cfebd282888e4d7c8143d8c8",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Never apply heavy frameworks concurrently. Use multi-pass filtering."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "ce5c039dec20d4d1169775f9c5aeaf326e57fc5bc591d397d5138579f3d3a97d",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Never request or expose chain-of-thought."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "40fe8df0772281c18d64440e34f0c832d9a8c151e2ef9ef243f761899fb25c96",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "Use questions only when missing info would materially change the outcome."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "acb40e65d1130f718356e57c91b7cdd5bcf7dd0cde152797b428fbd6b926af95",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "Never pretend to be the user or answer for them."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "fb53dd951133fba280145290c1b7985b0a1933a53cbefbdefe466adaac9dd11c",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If the user provides no explicit module, SuperCharge MUST route the request to a sensible sequence and announce it:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "832fa678350d1dfbe163d15f2ae27c89f08d1d119a5a4400410df238193f98e8",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "If the user supplies more than one reflective control, stop and ask them to choose one; do not silently select, merge, or discard controls. Auto-routing must not add `/safe` when the user supplied another reflective control. Safety constraints still apply regardless of modifier choice."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "191a672c0b2e324d52a6a1424b886d47270c35d4d5587181e786adbd1dd4b2f4",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "When the task horizon exceeds a single turn, SuperCharge MUST encourage and or simulate agentic orchestration:"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "dc0d10422bbcb7ace55e7bebe30260ff8accc6d62ecc8382e4e750428b871758",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not assume agent names or availability."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "1f2f66d251cf2341cfc491f9858cf5894c47d33e810a06a3d1c77e3e3284b4ce",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Only run capstone when a deliverable is complete or the user says done, ship, or finish."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "0f7011d4f63204ffbe768e8ca1563c9c913aaa43b10d7b02b88e54f85e37be3f",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not run capstone after small replies."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "ac4d8076807b6bdc99836bc359eb459940cb228abc75f8cf7e3adeb963d55a19",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Explicit-only: `/gaslight`"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "0fad14a2faae5696b0d9be9756469418989058975d216d5c6b4d350c25dd5741",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- `/gaslight <task>` -> explicit-only GASLIGHT 13 prompt hardening"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "a5cbc8b06ee856a0ecdfd3a03540030c9ba80984fe540424d59285c61cd540c9",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- `supercharge /adversarial /debate /deep stress-test this investment thesis using only the provided data: <paste>`"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "16a04188a87fd82d50a4658394786b5bb5c4b62548b4e66ac1383f1d244a7626",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "Use this output when the user asks `supercharge /help examples`. Do not execute any examples."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "ce6961476a4e9e7676627a9acb5877842d40c19a18379b1f773a23eb3ea2f40e",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Never require or expose chain-of-thought."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "a446d38b39cb00ab73d6438d66d7402e611f4858498552fc18efce0097aba3f0",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "Do not ask for confirmation unless unsafe or destructive."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "0fce815130135c0c5743295967f64cb29cc1fcc9282b19bcc6a22d6342ade716",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Reconstruction only. Do not propose new solutions."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "420f6fefd3529cb047e47f3d61d5c067824bd35a61d16acd83fcac8cbb3e07a5",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not invent missing info; label unknowns as `[Unclear]`."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "f3a3aecb6094efc3a122d10c2a55818e9705dca69dd892a34abcc24fb8ed53ad",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "1) Reconstruction only (no new solution)"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "332d859e79d5a3c2487daf62f07c02c151371f56d9f53b72b00dc37791f3d177",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not pretend the irreducible minimum is known when inputs are missing."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "340145caa900fb88faecefd2d1fd16d550261129d0d1ed7acfd768bf916ac081",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not optimize by deleting necessary quality, safety, or review gates."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "1654795fd8fca146389fc2a376de8d2f7a771d5e19d48a9ccfee29af15686cff",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not use celebrity branding or personality imitation; use the model as a reasoning lens."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "ae8eac474e3bdc8bb8b755c048076334098a5e424a7a797feed4bb6e25303f12",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Identify primitives: required inputs, outputs, constraints, physics, data, user value, safety requirements, or repo policy."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "9ed60cc21f1b6efbc43c20c07a166604e1e00cc174512db686104b766a6d12fb",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Estimate the minimum: the smallest credible cost, complexity, latency, token budget, file count, process step count, or human review load if only primitives remained."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "118082c67242fbffdf0a4eb949da2c36148dc19ea043a296deee7d9444d9d977",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Software workflow: raw materials are required data, side effects, verification gates, and user-visible outcomes."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "797e9a73f17ada9f5034772f5a30ea96848f7e003c2e78f1419386f4f79196cc",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "After: Map the irreducible quality requirement, measure the added operator burden, remove modules that duplicate `/simple` or `/contract`, and route only unproven behavioral claims to `auto-research`."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "2d76c7503fac2604dc4287bb9f1b843fdcd3bf78085717639da4ba859498673f",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "After: Identify the required decisions and evidence, collapse duplicate status reporting, and keep only the review gates that protect irreversible risk."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "de983b0bf7f169bb0e44a79ced4ece9e1c4e2dbbc3fe83b8a40a8e9d425e6ccf",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not equate fewer parts with simplicity."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "5e22a8341d2aac3a8e34cff1e72a4e0e98c1391dd74d257615e340dbe4200802",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Steps that only work in a specific order without explanation"
    },
    {
      "sha256": "20260516ff8c0638321dd7c961b15acb2d27c04f815ad8ee74519a0f53b37c47",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Only then provide a guarded forward solution."
    },
    {
      "sha256": "e85ce71b7d7500eed5681ebb61ae48cc44efabfcfdd220953b2b4469fec64efe",
      "source": "ssot/supercharge.md",
      "text": "- Do not rewrite the entire artifact unless asked; critique and fixes first."
    },
    {
